  "asr_text": "It is like someone saying, I won't drive while helping put fuel in a car. Not taking the wheel is different from not supporting the journey. But this comparison cannot settle who is responsible for military support. What we need to check is what the words cover. So, if you sum it up as Britain won't attack, you stretch what was said about the Typhoon mission too far, making it cover all support. On the other hand, looking at what the refueling support covers and saying, then the Typhoons will attack too, goes beyond the evidence. The tools you need to read news are not a magnifying glass, but three questions: Who, for which mission, doing what? Don't leave after seeing only the big sign that says to protect, check the name tag underneath it too. Just putting one subject back can change how the news looks.",
